# GeT-RM reference material, Coriell ID GM16688. GeT-RM consensus diplotype:
# *2/*3 -- a real compound-heterozygous sample carrying both no-function
# alleles at once, tested with 3 methods (Roche AmpliChip, AutoGenomics
# INFINITI, Luminex xTAG). This is a real-world instance of the "no
# PharmVar-defined cis-compound allele combines these two SNPs" reasoning
# in genes/cyp2c19.py's module docstring: the lab consensus itself reports
# this as a direct *2/*3 diplotype (Poor Metabolizer), not a phasing
# caveat. Source: Pratt VM et al. 2010, J Mol Diagn 12:835-846
# (PMID 20889555), as reproduced in CDC's public-domain data table
# (https://www.cdc.gov/lab-quality/media/pdfs/2024/08/CYP2C19_GeneConsensus.pdf,
# retrieved 2026-08-18). Genotype below constructed from this project's own
# dbSNP-confirmed defining-variant coordinates (genes/cyp2c19.py), not
# redistributed from GeT-RM/Coriell/CDC directly.
#CHROM	POS	ID	REF	ALT	QUAL	FILTER	INFO	FORMAT	SAMPLE1
